card c14
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: what can change it?
figure: flame-and-ice
figure_at: 1

body:
    An unstable nucleus is called a [[radionuclide|radionuclide]]. When it changes, a different nuclide can result, and energy leaves as particles or electromagnetic radiation. Heating, cooling and chemistry hardly change how fast this happens. In a flame or in ice, it is still unstable.
